^["intent"]{
 ~#goal: "No grammar change surprises a corpus: its drift is a list before it lands and a count in its receipt after"
 ~#taste: "Read the consumer in place, keep only fingerprints; a reading that changes is reported whether the change is a fix or a regression"
}

^["open"]{
 # Unresolved questions. When resolved: log in stream, then move to ^["done"] as ~#resolved(label).
 ?[fingerprint_grain]: "Is a line's reading the top expression that starts on it, or every node whose span starts on it? The first is stable to read; the second catches a slot that moved inside a body."
 ?[verb_home]: "spw readings as its own verb, or --readings on fingerprint, which already counts node types per surface?"
 ?[snapshot_home]: "Where does a corpus snapshot live: the scratch of the run that takes it, .spw/gen here, or beside the consumer's own generated files?"
}

^["commits"]{
 # Named, in order. Planned ~[name]; landed .[name](hash). Names are never reused.
 ~[line_reading_fingerprint]: "&[seed] — a reading fingerprint per line: node kind, slots in written order, medial arms, and the lines the construct spans; whitespace and comments do not change it"
 ~[readings_snapshot]: "&[cli] — write the fingerprints of a corpus to a snapshot with the parser revision and corpus revision beside them"
 ~[readings_check]: "&[cli] — compare a corpus with a snapshot and list each line whose reading changed, old and new, with counts by kind; exit nonzero on any change unless --expect names it"
 ~[corpus_by_path]: "&[cli] — read a corpus by explicit path outside this repo (a mounted consumer, read in place), keeping only fingerprints and counts"
 ~[release_readings]: "#[release] — each parser release carries the readings of a fixed specimen set in its manifest, so two releases compare by diff (with parser-releases)"
 ~[grammar_receipt]: ".[commit-review] — a commit that changes a reading cites its drift in *[verify]: lines changed per corpus"
}

^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-11-06 17:24] observe — Four silent misreads found by one-off censuses the same day: line-crossing medial capsules (10 here, 347 in a mounted consumer), key = value as three loose expressions (most of 2,174 lines here, 25,429 there), key = @handle as a bias edge (27 here, 2,590 there), and <…> after an operation's slots (0 here, 28 there). Each fix changes existing readings; nothing in the repo can list them. The consumer verifies its own reader with a manifest snapshot compared before and after a change.
 >>[2026-11-06 17:24] decide — A plan of its own: it gates every grammar change in brace-slot-reading, plan-stream-parse-health and syntax-hardware-alignment, and gives parser-releases the artifact spw.quest's two-release specimen view waits on.
}

